257
00:15:58,120 --> 00:16:01,000
And who knows what science will come up with in the future...

258
00:16:01,160 --> 00:16:05,880
...but, Chandler, what if I die an unsuccessful, regular-size man?

259
00:16:07,920 --> 00:16:10,880
Hey, Monica. Wow, you've been in the bathroom for, like, a half-hour.

260
00:16:11,880 --> 00:16:13,630
I know.

261
00:16:13,930 --> 00:16:15,640
Had the beef tips, huh?

262
00:16:27,520 --> 00:16:29,360
Hey.

263
00:16:33,490 --> 00:16:35,280
You ate meat!

264
00:16:37,320 --> 00:16:38,370
You had sex!

265
00:16:41,080 --> 00:16:42,700
- No, we didn't.     - I know you didn't.

266
00:16:42,870 --> 00:16:45,160
I was talking about Monica.

267
00:16:46,580 --> 00:16:48,040
Phoebe, I did not have sex.

268
00:16:48,210 --> 00:16:51,130
Oh, this pregnancy is throwing me all off.

269
00:16:51,630 --> 00:16:54,090
- I'm gonna say hi to the chick and duck.     - Oh, me too.

270
00:16:54,590 --> 00:16:57,300
Why would you need to say hi? You've been feeding them for four days.

271
00:16:57,470 --> 00:17:00,560
Oh, right. Maybe I'll just go home.

272
00:17:11,030 --> 00:17:12,480
Well, we certainly are alone.

273
00:17:12,650 --> 00:17:14,820
Good thing we have that "not New York" rule.

274
00:17:14,990 --> 00:17:16,400
Right.

275
00:17:17,280 --> 00:17:19,990
Um, listen, since we're on that subject...

276
00:17:20,160 --> 00:17:23,660
...um, I just wanted to tell you that, um...

277
00:17:23,910 --> 00:17:26,580
Well, I was going through a really hard time in London...

278
00:17:26,750 --> 00:17:30,750
...what with my brother getting married and that guy thinking I was Ross' mother.

279
00:17:30,920 --> 00:17:32,090
Right.

280
00:17:33,550 --> 00:17:35,630
Well, anyway, I just...

281
00:17:35,880 --> 00:17:39,430
That night meant a lot to me. And I guess I'm trying to say thanks.

282
00:17:43,680 --> 00:17:46,100
You know, that night meant a lot to me too.

283
00:17:46,270 --> 00:17:48,850
And it wasn't because I was in a bad place or anything.

284
00:17:49,020 --> 00:17:53,020
It just meant a lot to me because you're really hot.

285
00:17:57,570 --> 00:18:00,030
- Is that okay?     - Ha, ha. That's okay.

286
00:18:01,080 --> 00:18:02,120
And I'm cute too?

287
00:18:04,660 --> 00:18:07,580
- And you're cute too.     - Thank you.

288
00:18:07,750 --> 00:18:10,790
- All right, I got to go unpack.     - Okay.

289
00:18:14,000 --> 00:18:15,380
Bye.

290
00:18:28,270 --> 00:18:30,650
I'm still on London time. Does that count?

291
00:18:32,230 --> 00:18:34,400
- Oh, that counts.     - Oh, good.

292
00:18:42,570 --> 00:18:43,950
Rach.

293
00:18:44,120 --> 00:18:46,040
- Rach.     - Hi.

294
00:18:46,200 --> 00:18:47,790
What are you doing here?

295
00:18:47,960 --> 00:18:51,370
Well, I've been on standby for a flight home for hours.

296
00:18:51,540 --> 00:18:54,420
- Oh.     - Oh. So no sign of Emily, huh?

297
00:18:54,960 --> 00:18:56,380
Not yet.

298
00:18:58,840 --> 00:19:00,550
So, um...

299
00:19:01,680 --> 00:19:03,300
What time are you supposed to leave?

300
00:19:03,470 --> 00:19:07,390
This is the last call for Flight 1066 to Athens.

301
00:19:07,560 --> 00:19:09,060
The last call.

302
00:19:09,230 --> 00:19:11,270
Pretty soon, I guess.

303
00:19:13,650 --> 00:19:15,310
I'm sorry.

304
00:19:16,650 --> 00:19:19,570
I just... I don't understand. I mean, how could she do this?

305
00:19:19,740 --> 00:19:22,200
What, am I like a complete idiot...

306
00:19:22,360 --> 00:19:24,410
...for thinking she'd actually show up?

307
00:19:24,580 --> 00:19:25,870
No.

308
00:19:26,030 --> 00:19:28,200
You're not an idiot, Ross.

309
00:19:28,370 --> 00:19:30,200
You're a guy very much in love.

310
00:19:31,210 --> 00:19:32,580
Same difference.

311
00:19:32,750 --> 00:19:37,880
All passengers for Flight 1066 to Athens should now be onboard.

312
00:19:38,050 --> 00:19:39,920
I get it!

313
00:19:44,050 --> 00:19:45,850
Well, that's that.

314
00:19:46,640 --> 00:19:48,140
No, you know what?

315
00:19:48,310 --> 00:19:49,640
I think you should go.

316
00:19:50,560 --> 00:19:52,940
- What?     - Yeah, I do think you should go...

317
00:19:53,100 --> 00:19:55,770
...by yourself. Get some distance.

318
00:19:55,940 --> 00:19:58,480
Clear your head. I think it would be really good.

319
00:19:58,650 --> 00:20:00,440
Oh, I don't know.

320
00:20:00,610 --> 00:20:03,400
Oh, come on, Ross. I think it would be really good for you.

321
00:20:05,780 --> 00:20:07,620
I could. I could do that.

322
00:20:07,780 --> 00:20:09,160
Yeah.

323
00:20:09,490 --> 00:20:12,080
I can't even believe her.

324
00:20:12,250 --> 00:20:14,250
You know what? I am going to go.

325
00:20:14,420 --> 00:20:15,500
- Good.     - Why not?

326
00:20:15,670 --> 00:20:17,380
- Right?     - Right. Right.

327
00:20:17,540 --> 00:20:20,130
- Thanks.     - Okay, I'll see you back at home.

328
00:20:20,300 --> 00:20:22,380
If I ever get a flight out of here.

329
00:20:22,550 --> 00:20:23,970
Hey, well...

330
00:20:24,640 --> 00:20:27,600
- No.     - What? Wait, what?

331
00:20:29,310 --> 00:20:30,770
Why don't you come?

332
00:20:30,930 --> 00:20:33,890
I mean, I have two tickets. Why not?

333
00:20:35,190 --> 00:20:39,440
Well, I don't know, Ross. Really?

334
00:20:39,860 --> 00:20:42,610
Yeah, yeah. It'd be great. I mean, you can...

335
00:20:42,780 --> 00:20:44,150
You can lay on the beach...

336
00:20:44,320 --> 00:20:47,910
...and I can cry over my failed marriage.

337
00:20:48,080 --> 00:20:50,700
- You see how I make jokes?     - Uh-huh.

338
00:20:51,330 --> 00:20:52,620
Really. I mean...

339
00:20:53,500 --> 00:20:55,040
God, I could use a friend.

340
00:20:55,330 --> 00:20:58,880
Oh, wow. Okay, maybe.

341
00:20:59,040 --> 00:21:00,420
Um...

342
00:21:01,380 --> 00:21:02,630
Yes, I can do that.

343
00:21:03,380 --> 00:21:05,510
All right, cool.

344
00:21:07,470 --> 00:21:09,600
Okay, we're going to Greece. Yeah, okay.

345
00:21:09,760 --> 00:21:11,760
Aah, aah. I forgot my jacket.

346
00:21:11,930 --> 00:21:14,230
- Well, you tell them to wait.     - Okay.

347
00:21:14,390 --> 00:21:16,480
- Wait. Wait.     - Okay.

348
00:21:21,150 --> 00:21:23,150
Emily.

349
00:21:28,030 --> 00:21:29,160
Oh, no, no, no.

350
00:21:30,950 --> 00:21:32,910
No! No!

351
00:21:33,080 --> 00:21:34,700
Emily!

352
00:21:37,870 --> 00:21:40,500
Ah, yes. I will have a glass of the Merlot...

353
00:21:40,670 --> 00:21:43,380
...and he will have a white-wine spritzer.

354
00:21:50,680 --> 00:21:52,350
Hey, look at that. The airport's moving.

355
00:21:53,810 --> 00:21:54,970
Hey, are we moving?

356
00:21:55,140 --> 00:21:57,310
Are we moving? Why are we moving?

357
00:21:57,480 --> 00:21:58,560
They... Um...

358
00:21:58,730 --> 00:22:01,860
Yeah, does the captain know that we're moving?

359
00:22:03,530 --> 00:22:04,530
Oh, my gosh.

